I began today's session with a coding challenge on Codewars.
These were the instructions:
Given two integers a and b (which can be positive or negative), find the sum of all 
the integers between and including them.If the two numbers are equal, return a or b.

First, I checked if a and b are equal; if so, the function returns a.
Then, I ensured that the starting number is always less than the ending number using 
min() and max().
After that, I stored the total number of terms in a variable called n and returned the sum 
of the numbers using the Gauss summation formula.

Even though my formula already handles the edge case where a and b are equal, I still 
implemented an if statement to make the code more readable and understandable for others. 
This also improves performance slightly by avoiding unnecessary calculations.
